// Development Jenkinsfile: tests the ansible-ci library straight from its git repository, WITHOUT
// registering it in Manage Jenkins > Global Pipeline Libraries.
// The pipeline expects the collection at the ROOT of the job repository (it is checked out into the src/
// sub-directory of the workspace, reports/ and dist/ beside it): use it in a repository that
// contains only this collection, renamed to `Jenkinsfile` (tools/export-collection.sh does both).
//
// Which library version is loaded: the part after '@' in `identifier`:
//   'ansible-ci@master'         a branch (here: the development branch)
//   'ansible-ci@v2.1.1'         a tag (needs gitTagDiscovery() below)
//   'ansible-ci@<40-char sha>'  an exact commit
// libraryPath: the library is in a sub-directory of the ansible-collection-ci repository.
//
// Variant, when this Jenkinsfile lives in the same repository as the library and you want to test the
// very same commit: retriever: legacySCM(scm: scm, libraryPath: 'jenkins-shared-library/')
// (only useful if that repository also has the collection at its root).
//
// Sandbox: a library loaded with `library` is UNTRUSTED and runs in the Groovy sandbox, unlike the trusted
// global library. ansible-ci only uses whitelisted calls (validated on Jenkins 2.580.1, no script approval);
// if a future change needs one, an admin approves it in Manage Jenkins > In-process Script Approval.
// Quick edits without a commit: open a build > Replay, edit the library script there, then Run.
library identifier: 'ansible-ci@master',
        retriever: modernSCM(
            scm: [$class: 'GitSCMSource',
                  remote: 'https://gitlab.corp.local/ci/ansible-collection-ci.git',   // PLACEHOLDER: library repository
                  credentialsId: 'git-readonly',                                       // read-only Jenkins credential
                  traits: [gitBranchDiscovery(), gitTagDiscovery()]],
            libraryPath: 'jenkins-shared-library/')

ansibleCollectionPipeline()
